  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/adro/Substance_Oxymetholone_Methasterone_LTM">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/adro/Metabolite"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">18-nor-17β-hydroxymethyl-17α-methyl-2α-methyl-5α-androst-13-en-3-one</rdfs:label>
    <adro:isMetaboliteOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/adro/Substance_Oxymetholone"/>
    <adro:isMetaboliteOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/adro/Substance_Methasterone"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The deciding body recorded that the parent substance cannot be determined between those named. Both are asserted; neither is asserted to the exclusion of the other.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">As stated in National Anti-Doping Panel (United Kingdom) SR/056/2022: either oxymetholone or methasterone could be a parent substance of the Metabolite; it is not scientifically possible to specify which of the two was in fact the relevant parent.</rdfs:comment>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>National Anti-Doping Panel (United Kingdom) SR/056/2022</obo:IAO_0000119>
  </rdf:Description>
